<%# Read-only display of the invoice master data (B3, doc/billing_stammdaten_plan.md §8).
    Local: account.

    Deliberately NOT shared with the admin display (B4): the admin area follows its own
    style guide. What IS shared is the value object Accounts::BillingAddress, so the postal
    ORDER of the lines can never drift between the two surfaces.

    The verification state of the VAT ID is not shown here on purpose: nothing sets it
    before the Stripe phase, so every row would read "unchecked" and turn a normal field
    into an apparent problem. It arrives with the webhook that can actually change it.

    Full i18n keys, not lazy `t('.x')`: the keys live under `views.billing_accounts.*`
    (CLAUDE.md key convention), which lazy lookup would not reach. %>
<dl class="text-sm border-b border-cream-200">
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-1 md:gap-8 py-4 border-t border-cream-200">
    <dt class="font-bold text-cream-900"><%= t('views.billing_accounts.details.address_label') %></dt>
    <dd class="md:col-span-2 text-cream-700">
      <%# The partial now also renders for an account carrying only a reference or a cc
          address (see the gate in show.html.erb), so the rows it always shows need an
          explicit empty state instead of a silently blank line. %>
      <% if account.billing_address.present? %>
        <% account.billing_address.lines.each do |line| %>
          <div><%= line %></div>
        <% end %>
      <% else %>
        <span class="text-cream-500"><%= t('views.billing_accounts.details.not_set') %></span>
      <% end %>
    </dd>
  </div>

  <% if account.vat_id.present? %>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-1 md:gap-8 py-4 border-t border-cream-200">
      <dt class="font-bold text-cream-900"><%= t('views.billing_accounts.details.vat_id_label') %></dt>
      <dd class="md:col-span-2 text-cream-700 font-mono"><%= account.vat_id %></dd>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-1 md:gap-8 py-4 border-t border-cream-200">
    <dt class="font-bold text-cream-900"><%= t('views.billing_accounts.details.email_label') %></dt>
    <dd class="md:col-span-2 text-cream-700">
      <%= account.billing_email.presence ||
          tag.span(t('views.billing_accounts.details.not_set'), class: 'text-cream-500') %>
      <% if account.billing_email_cc.present? %>
        <div class="text-cream-600">
          <%= t('views.billing_accounts.details.email_cc_prefix') %> <%= account.billing_email_cc %>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </dd>
  </div>

  <% if account.billing_reference.present? %>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-1 md:gap-8 py-4 border-t border-cream-200">
      <dt class="font-bold text-cream-900"><%= t('views.billing_accounts.details.reference_label') %></dt>
      <dd class="md:col-span-2 text-cream-700"><%= account.billing_reference %></dd>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</dl>
